186049069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1031 "Using Integration by Parts to Calculate Integrals With Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1033 1140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050521 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5036af57-460d-5886-bb25-967e885ae634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1031 "Differentiating Logarithmic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1033 1116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050690 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5f59a4ad-6d31-5757-be65-f24e070b2c60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1033 317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7280f087-059d-5524-8f8b-a1fe79b4ef9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096427 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096427 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12811582-7156-5b84-9ba9-5545f87894f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096427 #edb/ref 1074 "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096475 #edb/ref 1069 "e-493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096475 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7373a16-c90a-5875-8b17-8724542b35ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096475 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096476 #edb/ref 1069 "e-494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096476 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096476 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "672d52f6-89d8-550d-863b-7c5157d59ca3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096476 #edb/ref 1074 "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096834 #edb/ref 1039 "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm" #edb/ref 17592