17592186045417] [17592186424992 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424992 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424993 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\,dx=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{5}]-\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}}{5}-(\\frac{{e}^{5}}{25}-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(5{e}^{5}-{e}^{5}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(4{e}^{5}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
